Ladybird accepts empty custom-property values with important priority.
Blink’s CSSVariableParser::ConsumeUnparsedDeclaration() accepts empty
CSSVariableData, and css_parsing_utils::MaybeConsumeImportant() marks
the declaration important independently of its value.

WebKit’s CSSParser::consumeTrailingImportantAndWhitespace() removes
the priority annotation. CSSParser::consumeCustomPropertyValue()
creates an empty CSSCustomPropertyValue with that priority.

Gecko’s DeclarationParserState::parse_value() parses the value before
calling parse_important() to mark its priority. VariableValue::parse()
accepts an empty custom-property value.
